course: dictionary
lesson: 6143
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Many words have more than one meaning. You can find the right one by reading the words around it, which is the context. «Milky tea» and «the Milky Way» use the same word, but the clues point to different meanings: one is a drink, the other is a vast group of stars.
explain: Milky has three main meanings: containing a lot of milk, white and cloudy like milk, or part of the name of our galaxy. Ask yourself what the sentence is about: a drink, a liquid, or the night sky? Then choose the meaning that fits.
explain: Capital letters are a clue too. «The Milky Way» with capitals is a name for our galaxy. «milky water» with a small m is an ordinary describing word for water that looks cloudy. Test your choice by swapping the meaning into the sentence and checking it still makes sense.
fact: Milky can mean containing a lot of milk, as in «milky tea».
fact: Milky can mean white and cloudy like milk, as in «milky water».
fact: «The Milky Way» is the name of our galaxy, a pale band of light across the night sky.
fact: In science, limewater turns milky when carbon dioxide is bubbled through it.
fact: Light pollution from cities hides the Milky Way from many people who live in towns.
exercise: «The Sun is one of billions of stars in our galaxy, the Milky Way.» What is the Milky Way? | A town with many stars | A drink people have before bed | A cloudy liquid used in science | *Our galaxy, a pale band of stars
exercise: «The limewater turned milky when the gas was bubbled through it.» What does milky mean here? | *White and cloudy, like milk | Our galaxy, full of stars | Containing a lot of milk | Very cold and icy
exercise: «He sipped his milky tea before bed.» What does milky describe? | *Tea made with a lot of milk | A dangerous path | A pale band across the sky | Water that is cloudy in a jar
test: «Galileo turned a small telescope on the Milky Way.» Which meaning of milky is used here? | White and cloudy like milk | Glowing softly in the dark | Containing a lot of milk | *Our galaxy, the name for the band of stars
test: «The water in the jar looked milky after the chemicals were stirred in.» What does milky mean? | Clear and sparkling | Containing a lot of milk, like a drink | The name of a galaxy | *White and cloudy, like milk
exam: Ruby says «the Milky Way» must be a drink because it has milky in it. What is the best reply? | It is a type of cloud in the sky | Milky means a drink, so Ruby is right | *The capital letters show it is a name, our galaxy in space | Milky means dangerous, so it must be a warning
